language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ calvin_puzzle: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Fill an n by n grid with the numbers 1 to n^2, each used once, starting from any square. The next number in the sequence is placed either vertically or horizontally exactly three squares away from the previous number (a two square gap between them), or diagonally exactly two squares away from the previous number (a one square gap between them).
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `calvin_puzzle.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/calvin_puzzle.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `calvin_puzzle_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py calvin_puzzle.json
$   savilerow model.eprime calvin_puzzle_1.param -run-solver

$ n: the grid is n rows by n columns
given n : int

$ squares are numbered by position: square (row r, column c) is number (r-1)*n+c
$ moves: the allowed pairs of squares [from, to] for a move between consecutive numbers: three squares straight up, down, left or right, or two squares diagonally
letting moves = [ [(r1-1)*n+c1, (r2-1)*n+c2] | r1 : int(1..n), c1 : int(1..n), r2 : int(1..n), c2 : int(1..n), ((|r1 - r2| = 3) /\ (c1 = c2)) \/ ((r1 = r2) /\ (|c1 - c2| = 3)) \/ ((|r1 - r2| = 2) /\ (|c1 - c2| = 2)) ]

$ x[r,c]: the number written in the square at row r, column c, indices 1-based
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of int(1..n*n)
$ square[k]: the position (numbered as above) of the square holding the number k (auxiliary)
find square : matrix indexed by [int(1..n*n)] of int(1..n*n)

branching on [square]
such that
$ every number from 1 to n^2 is written in exactly one square
allDiff(flatten(x)),
$ the square found for each number holds that number: square[x[r,c]] is the position of square (r,c)
forAll r : int(1..n) . forAll c : int(1..n) . square[x[r,c]] = (r-1)*n+c,
$ the positions of consecutive numbers are related by one of the allowed moves
forAll k : int(1..n*n-1) . table([square[k], square[k+1]], moves)
